Task: Vue adapter keyboard and ARIA + slider normalization + focus indicator
Phase: 3 (Framework Adapter Parity)
Scope: packages/vue/src/{Heelslide.vue,useHeelslide.ts,types.ts,style.css,HeelslideRender.test.ts} + 2 new test files

TDD: Red (15 failing of 21) -> Green (52 package specs passing).
tsc -b clean, oxlint clean.

Three things landed together because they touch the same element: slider
normalization, the ARIA completion, and the focus indicator. Splitting them
would have meant three passes over the same lines with the widget in an
inconsistent state between.

The focus-indicator fix is the one worth remembering. outline: none on
.heelslide-handle was harmless-looking, but the handle carried the only
tabindex - so the sole focusable element had its focus ring suppressed. Nothing
in the suite could have caught it, because nothing was focusable enough to
test. Moving focus to the container made the rule inert and let a real
indicator be added.

Pre-existing spec updated rather than worked around: HeelslideRender asserted
role="slider" on the handle. That is the divergence being fixed, so the
assertion was retargeted at the container rather than the change being bent to
preserve it.
